            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"REFINED\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"The consensus identifies love primarily as God's essential nature and the self-giving, sacrificial devotion to the well-being of others, which serves as the supreme Christian virtue, fulfills the divine law, and encompasses covenant loyalty.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"The book defines love specifically as self-giving, faithful obedience to God's law, asserting that true love cannot exist apart from obedience.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"God's essential nature of self-giving benevolence and the corresponding human devotion to God and neighbor.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"Faithful obedience to God's law in relationships with God and others.\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"BOOK_NARROWS\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"BOOK_SUBSET\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The book restricts the definition of love strictly to actions of obedience to God's law, whereas the consensus encompasses a broader range of meanings including God's ontological nature, interpersonal affection (philia), and unconditional benevolence, treating obedience as a primary outcome or expression of love rather than its exclusive definition.\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"There is no direct contradiction, as the consensus widely acknowledges that biblical love is inseparable from obedience and fulfills the law. The divergence lies in the book elevating obedience to the restrictive, definitional core of the term.\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The book takes a well-attested strand of the consensus—covenant loyalty and law-keeping (e.g., 1 John 5:3, John 14:15)—and makes it the exclusive matrix for defining love, thereby refining the concept to a narrower operational standard.\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"STRONG\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"By defining love exclusively as obedience to the law, the book may struggle to adequately explain texts where love is described as God's fundamental nature (1 John 4:8) before any law was given, or passages dealing with natural affection.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
